course: dictionary
lesson: 6047
title: Words in an emergency
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meningitis is a long word, but its context gives you clues. Read the sentence around it: «A rash that does not fade when you press a glass on it needs urgent medical help, because it can be a sign of meningitis, a very dangerous illness.» The words urgent, dangerous and illness tell you meningitis is serious.
explain: Look for more clues in the next sentence: «A rash that doesn't fade under a pressed glass, with fever, can mean meningitis or sepsis, very dangerous infections, and needs 999 or A&E straight away.» Two dangerous infections are named together, and the call to 999 shows you must act fast.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. Meningitis is a serious illness where the thin layers around the brain and spinal cord swell, usually because of an infection. Does that fit «a very dangerous illness»? Yes, so your meaning makes sense.
fact: Meningitis is a serious illness that affects the thin layers around the brain and spinal cord.
fact: It usually happens because of an infection, and the layers become swollen.
fact: Signs can include a high fever, a very bad headache, a stiff neck, dislike of bright light and being very sleepy.
fact: A rash that does not fade when you press a glass on it is an emergency sign. Vaccines protect against some kinds of meningitis.
fact: If you suspect meningitis, call emergency services quickly.
exercise: What is meningitis? | A sweet treat eaten after school | A kind of sports game played on grass | *A serious illness where the thin layers around the brain and spinal cord swell | A type of cloud that brings rain
exercise: «Teenagers get more jabs at secondary school, such as meningitis vaccines.» What do meningitis vaccines do? | Make you sleepy all day | Make bright light hurt your eyes | *Protect against some kinds of meningitis | Give you a stiff neck
exercise: Which of these is a sign of meningitis? | Hiccups for a minute | *A stiff neck | Itchy knees after football | Sunburnt nose
test: Meningitis is an emergency. What should you do if you suspect it? | *Call emergency services quickly | Give a sweet and let the child sleep | Sit in bright sunlight to feel better | Wait a week and see what happens
test: «A rash that does not fade when you press a glass on it.» What does does not fade mean here? | It goes white and disappears | It turns into a cold | It spreads to the arm | *It stays visible under the glass
exam: Which word names the illness where the thin layers around the brain and spinal cord swell? | Stiff | *Meningitis | Rash | Booster
